# Frontend Rules

Applies to React components, pages, hooks, and client UI only. Do not add server/database logic here.

## Scope

| In scope | Out of scope |
|----------|--------------|
| `src/components/**` | `src/app/api/**` |
| `src/app/**/page.tsx`, `layout.tsx` | Database queries, auth middleware |
| `src/hooks/**` | Server Actions with DB access |

## Components

- Functional components only; one component per file
- Colocate by role: `ui/`, `layout/`, `sections/`, `calculators/`
- Props typed with TypeScript interfaces; avoid `any`
- Use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` for conditional classes

## Styling

- Tailwind v4 only; use brand tokens: `brand-navy`, `brand-gold`, `brand-cream`, `brand-muted`
- Mobile-first; minimum body text 16px; tap targets ≥ 44px
- Section wrapper:

```tsx
<section className="py-16 md:py-24">
  <div className="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">{children}</div>
</section>
```

## Data & constants

- Import contact, nav, disclaimers from `@/lib/constants` — never hardcode phone/email
- Client components: add `"use client"` only when needed (hooks, motion, forms)

## Images & links

- Use `next/image` with descriptive `alt`
- External links: `target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"`
- Phone CTA: `href="tel:+919322887442"`

## Forms (client)

- React Hook Form + Zod; show accessible error messages
- Disable submit while pending; success/error feedback required

## Accessibility

- Semantic HTML (`nav`, `main`, `section`, `button`)
- Visible focus rings; labels on all inputs
- Senior-friendly: clear CTAs, no jargon without explanation

## Do not

- Fetch secrets or env vars meant for server-only use
- Put SQL, Prisma, or auth verification in components
- Use inline styles or raw hex when brand tokens exist
